{number: 28}
{title: While Shepherds Watched Their Flocks}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] While shepherds watched their [G] flocks by night,
All [C] seated [G7] on the [C] ground;
The angel of the [G] Lord came down,
And [C] glory [F] shone a-[C] round,
"Fear [G] not!" said he,
for [C] mighty dread had seized their [G] troubled mind.
"Glad [C] tidings of great [F] joy I bring
to [C] all of [G7] human-[C] kind."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
"To [C] you, in David's [G] town,
This day is [C] born of [G7] David's [C] line a Savior,
Who is Christ the [G] Lord,
and [C] this shall [F] be the [C] sign, and this shall be the sign:"
"The [G] heavenly babe you [C] there shall find
To human [G] view displayed,
All [C] meanly wrapped in [F] swathing bands,
And [C] in a [G7] manger [C] laid."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Thus [C] spake the seraph [G] and forthwith
ap-[C] peared a [G7] shining [C] throng
of angels praising [G] God on high,
who [C] thus ad-[F] dressed their [C] song:
"All [G] glory be to [C] God on high,
And to the [G] earth be peace;
Good [C] will henceforth from [F] heaven to earth
Be-[C] gin and [G7] never [C] cease!"
{end_of_verse}
